#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:3
msgid "Project scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:5
msgid ""
"pipx installs and runs Python applications. It manages the isolated "
"environments that support those applications and exposes their entry points "
"on ``PATH``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:10
msgid "What pipx manages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:12
msgid ""
"Persistent application environments for ``pipx install`` and disposable "
"environments for ``pipx run``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:13
msgid ""
"User installations by default and system installations when the caller "
"passes ``--global``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:14
msgid ""
"Application dependencies inside a managed environment. For unlocked "
"environments, ``inject`` and ``--preinstall`` extend an application "
"environment; they do not create standalone library environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:16
msgid ""
"Entry points from the main package and dependencies named with ``--include-"
"resources-from`` or ``--include-deps``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:18
msgid ""
"An install fails when neither the package nor its selected dependencies "
"expose an application. The caller can pass ``--app NAME`` to require an "
"exact entry point. pipx removes a new environment or restores an existing "
"one when the check fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:24
msgid "Boundaries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:26
msgid "pipx does not manage these use cases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:28
msgid "standalone environments for importing libraries or modules;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:29
msgid ""
"tool selection based on the current directory, parent directories, or "
"project metadata;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:30
msgid "system installation inferred from elevated privileges;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:31
msgid "a ``pip`` executable from each managed environment on ``PATH``;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:32
msgid ""
"package search, package ranking, or index-specific application discovery; or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:33
msgid ""
"frozen pipx executables, operating-system packages, zipapp installers, "
"repositories, and signing keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:35
msgid ""
"Use ``pipx runpip`` when you need package-manager access inside an "
"environment that pipx created. Distribution projects may package pipx for "
"their users, but each ecosystem owns its build, release, update, and signing "
"process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:40
msgid "Configuration and state"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:42
msgid ""
"Ordinary pipx commands do not search the current directory or its parents "
"for configuration. ``pipx manifest sync PATH`` applies the desired "
"application state from the manifest at ``PATH``; pipx does not infer that "
"path. The manifest accepts tool state instead of arbitrary command defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:46
msgid ""
"pipx can record an environment's resolved dependencies as a lock file in the "
"PyPA ``pylock.toml`` format, so the environment rebuilds identically; ``pipx "
"manifest lock`` writes these locks and ``pipx install --lock`` reads one "
"back. pipx does not use ``requirements.txt`` as a state or lock format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:50
msgid ""
"pipx exposes top-level policy when pip and uv honor the same contract. "
"Backend arguments carry controls specific to pip or uv. ``--cooldown DAYS`` "
"maps one pipx release-age policy to both backends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:53
msgid ""
"A release-age policy describes the machine, not one command, so "
"``PIPX_COOLDOWN`` supplies the default and no configuration file appears to "
"hold it. That keeps pipx settings in one place and keeps the policy out of "
"the backend environment variables (``PIP_UPLOADED_PRIOR_TO``, "
"``UV_EXCLUDE_NEWER``), which would bind pipx to one backend and leak into "
"unrelated pip and uv runs in the same shell. The variable outranks the "
"cooldown an environment recorded at install time, because it states what the "
"machine wants now rather than what an older install happened to use; ``--"
"cooldown`` still overrides both, and a lock file supersedes all of them by "
"pinning every version outright."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:60
msgid ""
"Application launchers start the installed application without downloading "
"packages or changing its environment. Health checks and repairs belong in "
"commands that the user invokes for those purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:65
msgid "Existing directory lookup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:67
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` has experimental support for applications under "
"``__pypackages__/<major>.<minor>/lib/bin`` in the current directory. This "
"behavior predates the scope above and conflicts with the directory-discovery "
"boundary. New features must not use it as a model; the project should "
"deprecate and remove it in a separate change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:73
msgid "Choose another tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/scope.rst:75
msgid ""
"Use a project dependency manager such as uv or Poetry for project libraries "
"and development tools. Use ``venv``, pip, or uv for a library environment. "
"Use a version manager such as mise when a directory must select tool "
"versions, and use the system package manager to find or install operating-"
"system packages."
msgstr ""
